course: dictionary
lesson: 8386
title: Rubble: broken pieces after a fall
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Rubble is the broken pieces of stone, brick and concrete that are left when a building falls down or is knocked down. Think of a wall after an earthquake: the heap of broken bits on the ground is rubble.
explain: «Rescue dogs can smell a person buried under snow or rubble.» The clue is buried: people are trapped under the broken pieces of a building. Ask yourself what word would fit there, then try your meaning, broken bricks and stones, in the sentence to check it makes sense.
explain: Rubble has a second job in building. «A bulldozer pushes earth and rubble with a big blade at the front.» Builders use rough broken stones to fill gaps or make a firm base under a path or a wall, so the word can describe a useful material as well as a disaster.
fact: Rubble means broken pieces of stone, brick and concrete.
fact: Rubble is uncountable, so say «some rubble» or «a pile of rubble», never «two rubbles».
fact: Useful phrases: «reduced to rubble», «search the rubble», «buried under rubble».
fact: In news about earthquakes and wars, rescuers search the rubble for survivors.
fact: In building, rubble is used as a firm base under paths.
exercise: «Rescue dogs can smell a person buried under snow or rubble.» What does rubble mean here? | Deep, cold water in a river | *Broken pieces of stone, brick and concrete from a fallen building | Thick, green grass in a field | Soft, dry sand on a beach
exercise: Which phrase means rescuers are looking through the broken pieces for people? | *search the rubble | reduced to rubble | rubble path | a pile of rubble
exercise: Which is correct, because rubble cannot be counted in ones? | a rubbles | *some rubble | three rubbles | two rubbles
test: In building, what is rubble used for? | *as a firm base under a path | to make paper | to make a sandcastle | as food for birds
test: «The town was reduced to rubble after the earthquake.» What does reduced to rubble mean? | *Destroyed and broken into pieces | Moved to a new place | Covered in snow | Rebuilt and painted
exam: Which sentence uses rubble correctly? | Rubble is a kind of bird that flies | The rubble are very tall | *The rescuers searched the rubble for survivors | The rubbles were searched for survivors
